# Jak II: every pad button in play (LIST-0.1.1 item 27; the owner: "make sure all mappings and functions work in all
# games"), made by C:\JakQuest\sim\make_buttons.sh. Into play as jak2_melee.sim, then from frame 4600: A (jump), B (spin kick),
# X (punch), the left trigger (crouch), A then X in the air (the dive), the left trigger and X (the
# uppercut), the stick ahead and X (a running punch), the left stick's click (L3), Y (Triangle) twice (Jak 1's
# look-around and out of it), the menu button (pause, then again once the menu is open: Jak II and 3 take no Start
# while it opens; play again once it has gone), the right grip at the hip (Jak II and 3: the gun drawn from its holster) and the right
# trigger (fired), the right stick's click twice (R2: Jak II and 3's JET-Board, on and off again), then the left grip
# (L2: Jak II and 3's Dark Jak, which takes no board; Jak II's test aid gives him dark eco; Jak 1 fists). Run with
# JAKVR_STATE_TRACE=1 (Jak II and 3 also JAKVR_TEST_GUN=1 JAKVR_TEST_BOARD=1 JAKVR_BODY_TRACE=1); expect in run.log the
# states target-jump, target-attack, target-running-attack, target-duck-stance, target-flop, target-attack-uppercut,
# "[vr-pad] Start", Jak II and 3's "[vr-gun] a round fired", target-board-start, Jak II's target-darkjak-get-on and
# Jak 3's target-powerjak-get-on.
